The module is already in the tree: baseq3/uix86.dll (md5 7f2b92700036167b1ab33cadba56fd8f, same build as the exe). It is proven on three boxes.

The changes live in:
- scripts/fleet/stage-fleetres.py (repair pair);
- the share-only FLEETGL.BAT and tests/python/test_q3_voodoo2_gl.py;
- scripts/benchmarks/lan_check.py.

Re-stage through gvfs and verify each file through /mnt. The optional server change is ~/q3a-server/.q3a/baseq3/server.cfg. Nothing needs downloading.

titles.verifier_notes:
CONFIRMED. I found nothing to refute: launch, menu table and the 640x480 label are hardware-confirmed on .195; retail launches are confirmed on all four boxes.

Added:
- the reasoning for why the zz pk3 cannot cause a kick;
- that the QVM route also covers ioquake3 local games at sv_pure 1;
- the sv_allowDownload option for server-side coverage.

The retail Apply trap itself was not demonstrated on hardware. .145's m8 'retail accept test' logged no vid_restart. It follows from the identical pak8 QVM, whose trap was measured under ioquake3 on all four boxes.
